course: dictionary
lesson: 6664
title: Nylon: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the context to choose the right one. Nylon is a noun, a name for a thing. «A strimmer's nylon string spins so fast it cuts like a blade» tells you nylon here means a thin, strong thread. The clue is the string, which is what the nylon is.
explain: Nylon is a strong, light, man-made material made from chemicals, a kind of plastic. Read this clue: «Nylon was invented in the 1930s to replace silk; it was cheaper and stronger.» So nylon is a material that people made to take the place of silk.
explain: Nylon can also mean something else in its plural form, nylons. In old-fashioned writing, nylons are thin stockings or tights made of nylon. Ask yourself, what word would fit here? If the sentence is about legs and getting dressed, the old meaning is the one you need.
fact: Nylon is a strong, light, man-made material made from chemicals.
fact: Nylon is used for clothes, ropes, toothbrush bristles, tents and fishing line.
fact: Nylon is a synthetic fibre, not a natural one like cotton or wool.
fact: Nylon was invented in the USA less than a hundred years ago.
fact: Nylon does not rot easily, so old fishing nets can stay in the sea and pollute it.
exercise: «A strimmer's nylon string spins so fast it cuts like a blade.» What is nylon here? | *A strong, man-made thread | A sort of wooden stick | A brightly coloured bird | A kind of fruit
exercise: «Nylon was invented in the 1930s to replace silk.» What was nylon made to take the place of? | Gold | Wool | *Silk | Rubber
exercise: Jayden says nylon is a natural fibre, like cotton. Is he right? | *No, nylon is man-made, made from chemicals | Yes, cotton and nylon are the same | Yes, it grows on plants | Yes, it is made from sheep's wool
test: In an old film, a lady pulls on her nylons before the dance. What are nylons? | Small bristles on a brush | A kind of dance | *Thin stockings or tights | Strong ropes for a boat
test: Why are old nylon fishing nets a problem in the sea? | *Nylon does not rot easily, so it pollutes the sea | Nylon turns into sugar in water | Nylon makes the water warm | Nylon is too light to sink
exam: «In a crash, sensors set off a small charge that fills a nylon airbag with gas in less time than a blink.» What does this tell you about the airbag? | *It fills with gas in less time than a blink | It is made of wood | It is only used on birds | It stays flat forever
